---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, personSchema } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Naman Goyal, B.S. (Research) physics undergraduate at IISc Bengaluru working in theoretical high-energy physics and mathematical physics." jsonLd={[personSchema]}
  ogImage="/og/about.png">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>{site.name}</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="about-grid section-tight">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I am an undergraduate student in the B.S. (Research) physics program at the Indian
          Institute of Science, Bengaluru, working in theoretical high-energy physics and
          mathematical physics. My interests center on the constraints that quantum field theory
          and symmetry principles place on physical theories, and on what effective descriptions
          can and cannot reproduce of the fundamental dynamics.
        </p>
        <p>
          In practice this has meant three lines of work. Classical tests of general relativity in
          pseudo-Newtonian frameworks, with Prof. Banibrata Mukhopadhyay at IISc, published as a
          preprint in 2026. Precision studies of electroweak vacuum stability, for which I built
          the <a href="/smvac/">SMVac</a> computational framework, together with the associated
          cosmological questions of Higgs initial conditions during inflation, with Prof. Rick
          Sandepan Gupta at TIFR. And since May 2026, scattering amplitudes and the S-matrix
          bootstrap at TIFR, asking whether the uniqueness of dual-resonance amplitudes can be
          established from analyticity, crossing symmetry, unitarity, and Regge behavior alone. A
          period of independent reading on Lorentz representations and the little group formalism
          underlies the more structural side of these interests.
        </p>
        <p>
          My methods combine analytical work with scientific computing: multi-loop renormalization
          group evolution, semiclassical decay calculations, numerical optimization, and parallel
          parameter scans. Alongside research, I have competed with the IISc team at the
          International Physicists' Tournament (National Runner-up, 2023 and 2024) and at PLANCKS
          (representing India, 11th place globally, 2024), and attended the Perimeter Institute
          Undergraduate Summer School in June 2026.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Contact.</strong> The best way to reach me is by email at
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>; my code lives on
          <a href={site.github} rel="me noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"> GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside>
        <img
          class="about-portrait"
          src="/portrait.jpg"
          alt="Portrait of Naman Goyal"
          width="750"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
